{"kind":"assert","text":"The proposal to stop world-staleness dragging healthy work projects stale from the moment it was appended, and this is the cleanest demonstration on the real log that the request asked for.\n\nMeasured at depth 1066: proposal f9f077ba, appended minutes earlier, reads stale=true. It rests on request 1e3c1cec and assert 4b56ec2e, both of which are themselves stale, so it inherited the flag transitively before any reader saw it. Nothing it describes has changed. No behaviour moved under it. The flag carries no information a reader could act on, and it is attached to the very act that asks for the flag to stop being attached this way.\n\nThis is the negative direction the request wanted demonstrated - a case that must not flare - and it costs nothing to observe because the fold produced it unprompted. The positive direction, a document flaring when the behaviour it describes changes, remains the property to preserve and is not affected by the proposed reading, since that relation would be declared as a describes edge.\n\nRecorded as evidence for whoever ratifies, not as a new finding: the mechanism is working exactly as specified, and the specification is what is under review."}